WEBVTT

00:00:00.556 --> 00:00:03.726
Every message you send
crosses an open channel.

00:00:04.226 --> 00:00:06.896
An attacker can watch it, or change it.

00:00:07.321 --> 00:00:09.771
Stallings splits these into two families.

00:00:11.589 --> 00:00:14.379
Passive attacks do not modify the data.

00:00:14.874 --> 00:00:16.124
They only observe.

00:00:16.739 --> 00:00:18.609
The threat is to confidentiality.

00:00:20.896 --> 00:00:23.486
Eavesdropping, also called interception.

00:00:24.206 --> 00:00:27.696
The attacker gains unauthorized
access to the data.

00:00:28.146 --> 00:00:31.616
Even encrypted content can
be read if the key leaks.

00:00:33.322 --> 00:00:35.352
Traffic analysis is subtler.

00:00:35.762 --> 00:00:39.972
The attacker observes patterns,
lengths and timing of messages.

00:00:40.687 --> 00:00:43.917
Even without reading content,
much can be inferred.

00:00:45.689 --> 00:00:48.519
Active attacks modify the data stream.

00:00:49.014 --> 00:00:50.424
They threaten integrity,

00:00:50.814 --> 00:00:52.464
authenticity and availability.

00:00:53.254 --> 00:00:55.184
The attacker does more than watch.

00:00:57.029 --> 00:00:59.999
Masquerade, also called impersonation.

00:01:00.459 --> 00:01:04.989
The attacker poses as another
entity to gain extra privileges.

00:01:06.922 --> 00:01:09.532
Replay, also called retransmission.

00:01:10.112 --> 00:01:15.882
Legitimate data is captured and sent
again to create an unauthorized effect.

00:01:17.589 --> 00:01:20.319
Modification alters the data stream.

00:01:20.819 --> 00:01:22.469
Messages can be deleted,

00:01:22.919 --> 00:01:26.149
reordered, delayed or have
their content changed.

00:01:27.756 --> 00:01:30.746
Denial of service prevents legitimate use.

00:01:31.261 --> 00:01:33.891
Flooding, jamming or crashing a resource

00:01:34.361 --> 00:01:35.971
so users cannot reach it.

00:01:37.556 --> 00:01:39.466
Attacks come through many surfaces.

00:01:40.171 --> 00:01:43.401
Application:
malware and cross site scripting.

00:01:43.851 --> 00:01:45.141
Operating system.

00:01:45.736 --> 00:01:48.446
Network: sniffing and denial of service.

00:01:48.991 --> 00:01:49.741
Physical.

00:01:50.346 --> 00:01:52.176
Human: social engineering.

00:01:53.989 --> 00:01:55.899
Passive attacks steal secrets.

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:58.244
Active attacks break trust.

00:01:58.854 --> 00:02:02.644
Knowing the surfaces is the
first step to defending them.

